## How the resource behaves

An appliance has exactly one set of backup settings, and it always exists (one setting is kept per
tenant; see *Tenancy*):

- **Create applies, destroy forgets.** Creating the resource applies the configured settings to the
  appliance's. Destroying it removes it from Terraform state only: the appliance keeps its settings,
  since there is nothing to delete or reset them to.
- **Only what you set is managed.** The provider sends only the settings in the configuration, and
  only those that change. An attribute you do not set keeps the appliance's value, and removing one
  from the configuration leaves the value on the appliance as it is.
- **Morpheus checks the values.** A default schedule or storage bucket id that does not exist is
  refused, and the apply fails with Morpheus' message. A setting Morpheus accepts but does not apply
  (see *Tenancy*) fails the apply with the setting's name and the value the appliance reports.
- **The appliance database backup.** Setting `backup_appliance = true` makes Morpheus create a
  backup job for the appliance database; `false` disables it. It is available to the master tenant
  only (see *Tenancy*).

## Tenancy

Morpheus keeps most of these settings once for the whole appliance, and one of them per tenant:

- **Appliance-wide** — `scheduled_backups`, `create_backups`, `retention_count` (and its alias
  `retention_days`) and `default_backup_schedule_id` are one value shared by every tenant. Any tenant
  whose role grants the backup-settings permission reads and changes the same value.
- **Per tenant** — `default_backup_storage_bucket_id` is each tenant's own default, chosen from the
  tenant's own storage buckets. It is the same flag as `hpe_morpheus_storage_bucket`'s
  `default_backup_target`, which defaults to `false`: a bucket managed in the same configuration
  must also set `default_backup_target = true`, or the two resources undo each other on every apply
  (see *Example Usage*). Alternatively, manage the default from one of the two resources only.
- **Master tenant only** — `backup_appliance`. There is one appliance backup for the whole appliance,
  managed by the master tenant. Morpheus accepts the setting from any tenant but, for a tenant other
  than the master, applies `true` to the master tenant's appliance backup, ignores `false`, and reports
  the setting as `false`. The provider therefore refuses `backup_appliance = true` when planning as a
  tenant other than the master (a warning instead, when it cannot determine the tenant), and fails an
  apply whose read-back shows a sent setting was not applied.

A bucket managed alongside the settings, with the flag set on both sides:

```terraform
resource "hpe_morpheus_storage_bucket" "backups" {
  name                  = "backups"
  provider_type         = "local"
  base_path             = "/var/opt/morpheus/morpheus-ui/backups"
  default_backup_target = true # the flag default_backup_storage_bucket_id sets below
}

resource "hpe_morpheus_setting_backup" "this" {
  default_backup_storage_bucket_id = hpe_morpheus_storage_bucket.backups.id
}
```

## Retention

`retention_count` is the number of successful backups to retain, 1 or more: Morpheus would store a
`0` but treats it as unset where it reads the retention (the appliance backup job falls back to 10),
so `0` and negative values are refused when planning. `retention_days` is a deprecated alias for the
same setting kept for compatibility with the previous version of the provider: despite its name it is
a number of backups, not days, and it has the same lower bound. The two are sent to one setting, so
they must not both be set, and whichever you set is mirrored into the other in state. `retention_days`
will be removed in the 2.6 release; use `retention_count`.

